# Every sidecar under tools/maps is read by tests and validators that compare bytes or generate files from them (test_score_monitors demands
# LF bytes in the monitors sidecars; core.autocrlf=true would check them out CRLF, which broke a fresh clone once). The index holds LF for all of
# them already (git ls-files --eol), so this rule changes no committed byte: it only fixes what a checkout writes (PLAN-YARD item 2).
tools/maps/**/*.json text eol=lf
